# Issue #3238 (rotation baselines larger than one request; greenfield flag
# day, no compatibility shim): each inline segment of a link-set mutation's
# `rotationBaseline` is one update, and is now held, whole, to the 16 MiB a
# sync request carries, where the route's own 32 MiB was its only bound. A
# response page serves one update within a 32 MiB share, so a segment near
# the route's ceiling could be accepted and, with its header, be more than
# any page serves. The SDK ships with the API and cuts a segment at 11 MiB of
# plaintext, which is under the bound once encoded. Delete these exact
# diagnostics, and this file, once main contains this contract.
POST /documents/{documentId}/link: request refinement 'request.post-link-rotation-baseline-segment-bytes' was added; existing clients were not rejected by it.
POST /documents/{documentId}/unlink: request refinement 'request.post-link-rotation-baseline-segment-bytes' was added; existing clients were not rejected by it.
